Investigate this Wazuh alert:

{
  "grouping_reason": "Default Domain Policy GPO modified to add a startup PowerShell script targeting all domain machines — coordinated modification within 60 seconds by service account svc_backup doing interactive admin work on the domain controller. The chain is: (1) SYSVOL file write of update.ps1 inside the Default Domain Policy folder, (2) Directory Service Event 5136 modifying the gPCMachineExtensionNames attribute on the GPO object (registers the Group Policy Client-Side Extension that will RUN the startup script), (3) SYSVOL file write of scripts.ini that REGISTERS update.ps1 as a startup script, (4) Directory Service Event 5137 creating a startup script extension entry. This is the EXACT signature of T1484.001 (Domain Policy Modification — GPO Modification) + T1547.001 (Boot/Logon Autostart via Startup Script). The blast radius is DOMAIN-WIDE: every machine that performs gpupdate /force OR reboots will pull the modified GPO and execute update.ps1 as SYSTEM at boot. svc_backup is a service account that normally runs Veeam/backup jobs non-interactively — it should NEVER modify Default Domain Policy interactively.",
